<article class="env-lemma" id="05XP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05XP">Lemma <span data-tag="05XP">97.12.2</span>.</a> In the situation of Lemma <a href="/tag/05XN" data-tag="05XN">97.12.1</a> assume that the given square is $2$-cartesian. Then the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{H}_ d(\mathcal{X}'/\mathcal{Y}') \ar[r] \ar[d] &  \mathcal{H}_ d(\mathcal{X}/\mathcal{Y}) \ar[d] \\  \mathcal{Y}' \ar[r] &  \mathcal{Y} }  \]
</div>
  <p> is $2$-cartesian. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We get a $2$-commutative diagram by Lemma <a href="/tag/05XN" data-tag="05XN">97.12.1</a> and hence we get a $1$-morphism (i.e., a functor) 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{H}_ d(\mathcal{X}'/\mathcal{Y}') \longrightarrow \mathcal{Y}' \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{H}_ d(\mathcal{X}/\mathcal{Y})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       We indicate why this functor is essentially surjective. Namely, an object of the category on the right hand side is given by a scheme $U$ over $S$, an object $y'$ of $\mathcal{Y}'_ U$, an object $(U, Z, y, x, \alpha )$ of $\mathcal{H}_ d(\mathcal{X}/\mathcal{Y})$ over $U$ and an isomorphism $H(y') \to y$ in $\mathcal{Y}_ U$. The assumption means exactly that there exists an object $x'$ of $\mathcal{X}'_ Z$ such that there exist isomorphisms $G(x') \cong x$ and $\alpha ' : y'|_ Z \to F'(x')$ compatible with $\alpha $. Then we see that $(U, Z, y', x', \alpha ')$ is an object of $\mathcal{H}_ d(\mathcal{X}'/\mathcal{Y}')$ over $U$. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>